{z}(1,2,-3) & =1(2)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈-6+⟨-6,-3,2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y-2,z+3⟩.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can estimate $f(1.01,1.95,-3.02)$ by evaluating the linear approximation at $x=1.01,y=1.95$ and $z=-3.02,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.01,1.95,-3.02) & ≈-6+⟨-6,-3,2⟩\\cdot ⟨1.01-1,1.95-2,-3.02+3⟩ \\\\  & =-6+⟨-6,-3,2⟩\\cdot ⟨0.01,-0.05,-0.02⟩ \\\\  & =-6-0.06+0.15-0.04 \\\\  & =-5.95\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335368 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335369 13194139535171 true] [17592186335368 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335370 13194139535171 true] [17592186335368 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335371 13194139535171 true] [17592186335368 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335372 13194139535171 true] [17592186335368 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335373 13194139535171 true] [17592186335368 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535171 true] [17592186335368 1041 "selection" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335368 1104 #edb/ref 17592186335373 13194139535171 true] [17592186335368 1110 #uuid "e7311abe-11fe-5247-ad21-d4ddf394da3a" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335369 1034 "-6.01" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335369 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535171 true] [17592186335369 1111 #uuid "67885177-68dc-55cb-8839-4576cc313a2a" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335370 1034 "-5.87" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335370 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535171 true] [17592186335370 1111 #uuid "8b7841f5-cf7f-5712-9062-5317389e0236" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335371 1034 "-5.98" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335371 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535171 true] [17592186335371 1111 #uuid "03007d32-556b-5252-b21a-ed92dbe88436" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335372 1034 "-6.12" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335372 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535171 true] [17592186335372 1111 #uuid "b9453ff8-2af8-5651-af0f-7977ae7f73d2" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335373 1034 "-5.95" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335373 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535171 true] [17592186335373 1111 #uuid "20bd1252-138f-5b02-bf93-781c065b83d2" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335374 1017 #edb/ref 17592186335375 13194139535171 true] [17592186335374 1089 "q-98544" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335374 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535171 true] [17592186335374 1100 "Let $f(x,y,z)=xy+xz+yz.$ Find the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,-2,-1).$" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335374 1113 #uuid "279eb0eb-b928-54d6-86d6-24d54146e691" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335374 1145 "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b,c)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈f(a,b,c)+∇f(a,b,c)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b,z-c⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,-2,-1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(1,-2,-1)+∇f(1,-2,-1)\\cdot ⟨x-1,y+2,z+1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the definition of $f,$ we have that $f(1,-2,-1)=-1.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x} & =y+z\\,⇒\\,{f}_{x}(1,-2,-1)=-3, \\\\ {f}_{y} & =x+z\\,⇒\\,{f}_{y}(1,-2,-1)=0, \\\\ {f}_{z} & =x+y\\,⇒\\,{f}_{z}(1,-2,-1)=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient of the function at the point $(1,-2,-1)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(1,-2,-1) & =⟨-3,0,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the linear approximation of the function $f$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(1,-2,-1)+∇f(1,-2,-1)\\cdot ⟨x-1,y+2,z+1⟩ \\\\  & =-1+⟨-3,0,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y+2,z+1⟩ \\\\  & =-1-3(x-1)+0(y+2)-1(z+1) \\\\  & =1-3x-z.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335375 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335376 13194139535171 true] [17592186335375 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335377 13194139535171 true] [17592186335375 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335378 13194139535171 true] [17592186335375 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335379 13194139535171 true] [17592186335375 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335380 13194139535171 true] [17592186335375 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535171 true] [17592186335375 1041 "selection" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335375 1104 #edb/ref 17592186335380 13194139535171 true] [17592186335375 1110 #uuid "271a2cfb-989d-5b0c-8b2e-977fd34bd876" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335376 1034 "f(x,y,z)≈1+3x-2z" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335376 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535171 true] [17592186335376 1111 #uuid "cf838683-3cfc-583a-becc-ba03ceffbdf6" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335377 1034 "f(x,y,z)≈4-3x-z" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335377 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535171 true] [17592186335377 1111 #uuid "013ef583-ef49-5ff0-a7f1-27f803debdf5" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335378 1034 "f(x,y,z)≈6-3x+y-z" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335378 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535171 true] [17592186335378 1111 #uuid "83bf3191-06c6-5f11-bc4a-d2520ecda92f" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335379 1034 "f(x,y,z)≈2-3x+y-z" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335379 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535171 true] [17592186335379 1111 #uuid "2fae9c02-7f10-5f28-be7c-2c0a0e60b499" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335380 1034 "f(x,y,z)≈1-3x-z" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335380 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535171 true] [17592186335380 1111 #uuid "0ea60411-f626-50d6-be65-ac915ce00c47" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335381 1017 #edb/ref 17592186335382 13194139535171 true] [17592186335381 1089 "q-98553" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335381 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535171 true] [17592186335381 1100 "Let $f(x,y)=x{e}^{y}.$ Find the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(-1,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2).$" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335381 1113 #uuid "02cd9397-a795-5b68-a5d4-f55d0d92f60a" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335381 1145 "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)≈f(a,b)+∇f(a,b)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(-1,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ≈f(-1,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)+∇f(-1,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)\\cdot ⟨x+1,y-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the definition of $f,$ we have that $f(-1,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)=-2.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x} & ={e}^{y}\\, &  & ⇒\\, & {f}_{x}(-1,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}=2, \\\\ {f}_{y} & =x{e}^{y} &  & ⇒\\, & {f}_{y}(-1,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)=-1{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient of the function at the point $(-1,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(-1,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & =⟨2,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the linear approximation of the function $f$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ≈f(-1,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)+∇\\,f(-1,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2⟩ \\\\  & =-2+⟨2,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2⟩ \\\\  & =-2+2(x+1)-2(y-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+2x-2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335382 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335383 13194139535171 true] [17592186335382 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335384 13194139535171 true] [17592186335382 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335385 13194139535171 true] [17592186335382 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335386 13194139535171 true] [17592186335382 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335387 13194139535171 true] [17592186335382 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535171 true] [17592186335382 1041 "selection" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335382 1104 #edb/ref 17592186335387 13194139535171 true] [17592186335382 1110 #uuid "76acc3b3-2256-500e-853d-ac36a9df1535" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335383 1034 "f(x,y)≈2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-x-y" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335383 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535171 true] [17592186335383 1111 #uuid "b2a6f096-41d9-5250-bd7e-b95d0b6e4a05" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335384 1034 "f(x,y)≈2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+2x+y" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335384 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535171 true] [17592186335384 1111 #uuid "9c3db9ab-4bdc-52c1-bd78-8d2f25ce180e" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335385 1034 "f(x,y)≈-2-x+y" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335385 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535171 true] [17592186335385 1111 #uuid "00243150-770f-5f4f-8449-bfc02dcdfce0" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335386 1034 "f(x,y)≈-2+2x-2y" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335386 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535171 true] [17592186335386 1111 #uuid "feb991f1-4050-58ab-86f0-3cb5c2eb15c0" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335387 1034 "f(x,y)≈2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+2x-2y" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335387 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535171 true] [17592186335387 1111 #uuid "daca5d82-050b-5f20-8c5f-4bab365f7108" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335388 1017 #edb/ref 17592186335389 13194139535171 true] [17592186335388 1089 "q-98555" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335388 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535171 true] [17592186335388 1100 "Let $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{9}{x+2y-z}.$ Find the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(2,1,1).$" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335388 1113 #uuid "ec12843c-221e-5977-accb-d9e9aa80cb79" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335388 1145 "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b,c)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈f(a,b,c)+∇f(a,b,c)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b,z-c⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(2,1,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(2,1,1)+∇f(2,1,1)\\cdot ⟨x-2,y-1,z-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the definition of $f,$ we have that $f(2,1,1)=3.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x} & =-\\frac{9}{(x+2y-z)^{2}}\\,⇒\\,{f}_{x}(2,1,1)=-\\frac{9}{(2+2(1)-1)^{2}}=-1, \\\\ {f}_{y} & =-\\frac{18}{(x+2y-z)^{2}}\\,⇒\\,{f}_{y}(2,1,1)=-\\frac{18}{(2+2(1)-1)^{2}}=-2, \\\\ {f}_{z} & =\\frac{9}{(x+2y-z)^{2}}\\,⇒\\,{f}_{z}(2,1,1)=\\frac{9}{(2+2(1)-1)^{2}}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient of the function at the point $(2,1,1)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(2,1,1) & =⟨{f}_{x}(2,1,1),{f}_{y}(2,1,1),{f}_{z}(2,1,1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,-2,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the linear approximation of the function $f$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(2,1,1)+∇f(2,1,1)\\cdot ⟨x-2,y-1,z-1⟩ \\\\  & =3+⟨-1,-2,1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,y-1,z-1⟩ \\\\  & =3-1(x-2)-2(y-1)+1(z-1) \\\\  & =6-x-2y+z.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335389 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335390 13194139535171 true] [17592186335389 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335391 13194139535171 true] [17592186335389 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335392 13194139535171 true] [17592186335389 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335393 13194139535171 true] [17592186335389 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335394 13194139535171 true] [17592186335389 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535171 true] [17592186335389 1041 "selection" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335389 1104 #edb/ref 17592186335390 13194139535171 true] [17592186335389 1110 #uuid "a212bf02-5f2e-5905-860c-5dcbb5c5bde6" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335390 1034 "f(x,y,z)≈6-x-2y+z" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335390 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535171 true] [17592186335390 1111 #uuid "c3edb51c-8bc1-5e43-a79b-4891054f59cd" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335391 1034 "f(x,y,z)≈8+x-2y-z" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335391 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535171 true] [17592186335391 1111 #uuid "1b35f050-d0ac-57fe-b923-292fbcac9a24" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335392 1034 "f(x,y,z)≈6-x+y-z" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335392 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535171 true] [17592186335392 1111 #uuid "c3ae3250-fa99-5810-ba7d-fc870a104f4b" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335393 1034 "f(x,y,z)≈8-x+y+z" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335393 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535171 true] [17592186335393 1111 #uuid "fae03db1-edc5-5270-8134-a60989997d41" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335394 1034 "f(x,y,z)≈6+x+2y-2z" 13194139535171 true] [17592186335394 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535171 true] [17592186335394 1111 #uuid "33064134-d89c-5a2d-9cf7-56b27083cd39" 13194139535171 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-129631" 17592186335304 "q-129631/selection" 17592186335305 "q-129631/selection/183f637f813799a89